      { "sa": "bhūta-bhāvanaḥ", "en": "bringing beings into being" }
    ],
    "translation": "And beings do not stand in me. See my lordly yoga. Bearing beings and not standing in beings, my self brings beings into being.",
    "notes": ["\"My self brings beings into being\" can also be read as \"I myself bring beings into being\"."]
  },
  "6": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "yathā", "en": "as" },
      { "sa": "ākāśa-sthitaḥ", "en": "standing in space" },
      { "sa": "nityam", "en": "always" },
      { "sa": "vāyuḥ", "en": "the wind" },
      { "sa": "sarvatra-gaḥ", "en": "going everywhere" },
      { "sa": "mahān", "en": "great" },
      { "sa": "tathā", "en": "so" },
      { "sa": "sarvāṇi", "en": "all" },
      { "sa": "bhūtāni", "en": "beings" },
      { "sa": "mat-sthāni", "en": "standing in me" },
      { "sa": "iti", "en": "thus" },
      { "sa": "upadhāraya", "en": "understand" }
    ],
    "translation": "As the great wind, going everywhere, always stands in space, so all beings stand in me. Understand it thus."
  },
  "7": {
    "words": [
